{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And YHWH saw that he turned aside to see.</b> We have received that there is a Name of one hundred and twelve letters and it goes forth from this verse, and it is a tradition of our master Shmuel ha-Kohen, may his memory be for a blessing, which he received from his master, and his master from his master, from the mouth of Rav Huna." "<b>Out of the midst of the bush.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: 'it is the bush (סנה), it is Sinai (סיני).' And so we may also interpret 'out of the midst of the bush (סנה)' as 'out of the midst of Nisan (ניסן),' for this vision appeared to Moses on the fifteenth of Nisan, and this is 'out of the midst of the bush' — that is, the day of redemption for the coming year, and you will need this again for a matter I am about to write." "<b>Moses, Moses.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): the reason they call a prophet from on high by a doubled name is that the voice had great power, in the manner of what is said (Psalms 29:4): ״קול ה׳ בכח״ — 'the voice of YHWH is in power' — and by virtue of the voice and its strength, the sound of the articulation was heard. And the calling of Moses was a single time, but it was heard by Moses as two times, and so for the rest of the prophets who were called by two times, in the manner of what is written (Psalms 62:12): ״אחת דבר אלהים שתים זו שמעתי כי עז לאלהים״ — 'one thing has Elohim spoken, two have I heard, that might belongs to Elohim' — that is, by virtue of the power of Elohim, for he hung the matter upon the power of the voice." "<b>And by way of</b> the Midrash: everyone whose name was doubled is in two worlds — Noaḥ Noaḥ, Avraham Avraham, Yaakov Yaakov, Moshe Moshe, Peretz Peretz. And behold, it is written Teraḥ Teraḥ — he too did not die until he had repented." "<b>And by way of</b> reason (sekhel): because the prophet who is called is startled by the first calling, and if the speech were to come to him immediately he would not understand it; therefore he needed to be called a second time, so that he might compose himself, and after that He would speak with him." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: the reason for the doubling in 'משה משה' and in the other prophets is to make plain that that calling, and all that follows from it, is all with the agreement of Mercy and Judgment. And the names called in the language of doubling from the Holy One, blessed be He — we do not find them in the Torah except four."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "Rendered 'one hundred and twelve letters' from מאה אותיות — but the Hebrew literally says 'one hundred letters'; בן appears to mean 'plus twelve' (i.e., 100 + 12 = 112), following the standard tradition of the 112-letter divine Name extracted from this verse; resolved by inference to the known tradition."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:55:53.407407316Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}